// What a '&uni' parameter points at is reached as 'uni': a mutable borrow of
// it freezes it entirely, so writing through the parameter while the borrow
// is still to be used is refused. This is Rust's '&mut' exclusivity, which in
// Cone is '&uni', not '&mut'.
//
// Verdict: refuse, ErrorFrozen at the write.
// Basis: refborref.html, "Freezing access to the source of a borrow" (a
// source reached as uni -- "what a uni reference points at"); Jon, 26 Sep
// 2026 (Backlog\types-pointers-and-borrowed-references.md): "Rust's &mut is
// Cone's &uni".
// Rust: 'fn f(p: &mut i64) { let a = &mut *p; *p = 7; *a = 1; }' is refused
// (E0506; by reading, not run).
// Master d331baab: correct.

mod lifetime_free_uni_param_frozen;

fn f(p &uni i64) i64 {
  imm a = &mut *p;
  *p = 7;                    //~ ErrorFrozen
  *a = 1;
  *p;
}
